.TH STOP-MU2E-SHIFT-SCHEDULER 1 "2026-08-31" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler v1.0.0" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler"
.SH NAME
stop-mu2e-shift-scheduler \- gracefully stop the running Mu2e Shift Scheduler server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./scripts/stop-mu2e-shift-scheduler
[\fB\-\-tail\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Stops the server started by
.BR start-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1).
Sends SIGTERM to the PID recorded in
.IR scripts/.mu2e-shift-scheduler.pid ,
waits up to 5 seconds for a clean exit, escalates to SIGKILL if needed, and
removes the PID file. Stale solver temp files older than one hour
(\fImu2e_sched_*\fR, \fImu2e_preview_*\fR, \fImu2e_staged_*\fR in the system
temp directory) are also cleaned up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tail
Print the last 20 lines of the server log before stopping.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I scripts/.mu2e-shift-scheduler.pid
PID of the running server.
.TP
.I scripts/logs/mu2e-shift-scheduler.log
Server log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-mu2e-shift-scheduler (1),
.BR bootstrap (1)
